71c5ec`. On the executor\\\\u2019s next return, `cmd_build` correctly found that driver-authored commit between `start_sha` and HEAD and refused the build as `no-cause`.\\\\n\\\\nThe operator\\\\u2019s read-only status question therefore changed the active build\\\\u2019s HEAD and invalidated an otherwise executor-authored build. The green forge checks do not cure this race, and the selected-test failure does not explain the recorded refusal.\\\\n\\\\n## Retires\\\\n\\\\nA read-only counsel/status inquiry, or transport of its record, being able to introduce a foreign commit into an active build\\\\u2019s commit range.\\\\n\\\\n## Change\\\\n\\\\nMake counsel/status recording and transport unable to mutate the checkout observed by an active build. Use an isolated transport worktree or defer the counsel-record commit until the active stage has produced its record. Preserve the build\\\\u2019s foreign-author guard; driver commits must not be silently exempted from it.\\\\n\\\\n## Acceptance\\\\n\\\\n- Start a two-iteration build whose first iteration creates an executor-authored commit and whose second iteration is still running.\\\\n- Run `attavo counsel N --ask \\\\\\\"how is it going so far?\\\\\\\"` and transport its record during that interval.\\\\n- The active build\\\\u2019s HEAD and executor commit range remain unchanged by the counsel operation.\\\\n- The build is not refused for the counsel record and can pass after its gates pass.\\\\n- The counsel record is eventually committed by the driver without being lost.\\\\n- An actual non-executor commit introduced into the build\\\\u2019s range remains refused by the existing authorship guard.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"forge\\\": {\\n    \\\"read\\\": true,\\n    \\\"reason\\\": null,\\n    \\\"checks\\\": [\\n      {\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"coherence\\\",\\n        \\\"conclusion\\\": \\\"success\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"name\\\": \\\"schema-version\\\",\\n        \\\"conclusion\\\": \\\"succes