l\": \"gpt-5.6-sol\"\n  },\n  \"adapter_version\": \"codex-cli 0.153.4\",\n  \"model\": \"gpt-5.6-sol\",\n  \"model_version\": null,\n  \"reports\": [\n    \"tokens\"\n  ],\n  \"tokens\": {\n    \"input\": 224827,\n    \"output\": 2743\n  },\n  \"cost_usd\": null,\n  \"wall_clock_s\": 73.272,\n  \"status\": \"done\",\n  \"class\": \"no-cause\",\n  \"verdict\": \"patch\",\n  \"citations\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"instruction\",\n      \"path\": \"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/cli.py\",\n      \"symbol\": \"counsel help: read-only; commits nothing\\u2014the caller commits, as with every stage\",\n      \"ruling_id\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"mechanism\",\n      \"path\": \"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/build.py\",\n      \"symbol\": \"cmd_build foreign-commit check\",\n      \"ruling_id\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"guard\",\n      \"path\": \"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/tests/test_counsel.py\",\n      \"symbol\": \"test_counsel_ask_reads_the_latest_record_even_when_it_passed\",\n      \"ruling_id\": null\n    }\n  ],\n  \"proposal\": {\n    \"ruling_text\": null,\n    \"patch\": null,\n    \"question\": null,\n    \"issue\": {\n      \"title\": \"A counsel status question can poison an active build with a foreign commit\",\n      \"body\": \"Severity: high / Provenance: product\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nItem 229\\u2019s executor committed the requested implementation at `15a774515f5a`. While build-01 was still active, `counsel --ask \\\"how is it going so far?\\\"` wrote counsel-01 and the driver committed it at `24aed171c5ec`. On the executor\\u2019s next return, `cmd_build` correctly found that driver-authored commit between `start_sha` and HEAD and refused the build as `no-cause`.\\n\\nThe operator\\u2019s read-only status question therefore changed the active build\\u2019s HEAD and invalidated an otherwise executor-authored build. The green forge checks do not cure this race, and the selected-test failure does not explain the recorded refusal.\\n\\n## Retires\\n\\nA read-only counsel/status inquiry, or transport of its record, being able to introduce a foreign commit into an active build\\u2019s commit range.\\n\\n## Change\\n\\nMake counsel/status recording and transport unable to mutate the checkout observed by an active build. Use an isolated transport worktree or defer the counsel-record commit until the active stage has produced its record. Preserve the build\\u2019s foreign-author guard; driver commits must not be silently exempted from it.\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n\\n- Start a two-iteration build whose first iteration creates an executor-authored commit and whose second iteration is still running.\\n- Run `attavo counsel N --ask \\\"how is it going so far?\\\"` and transport its record during that interval.\\n- The active build\\u2019s HEAD and executor commit range remain unchanged by the counsel operation.\\n- The build is not refused for the counsel record and can pass after its gates pass.\\n- The counsel record is eventually committed by the driver without being lost.\\n- An actual non-executor commit introduced into the build\\u2019s range remains refused by the existing authorship guard.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"forge\": {\n    \"read\": true,\n    \"reason\": null,\n    \"checks\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"coherence\",\n        \"conclusion\": \"success\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"schema-version\",\n        \"conclusion\": \"success\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"action-self-check\",\n        \"conclusion\": \"success\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"spec-gate\",\n        \"conclusion\": \"success\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"doctor\",\n        \"conclusion\": \"success\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"test\",\n        \"conclusion\": \"success\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"typecheck\",\n        \"conclusion\": \"success\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"question\": \"what is your recommendation?\",\